<div class="claim-alert"><div class="site-shell"><span>Active water entry or open roof?</span><a href="tel:+19808005991">Call now (980) 800-5991</a></div></div><header class="claim-header"><div class="site-shell"><a href="/" class="brand"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span><strong>MAJESTIC</strong><small>ROOFING, INC.</small></span></a><nav><a href="/">Home</a><a href="#first-steps">First steps</a><a href="#repairs">Repair options</a><a href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc">Claims</a></nav><a href="/es/reparacion-de-agujero-y-decking-charlotte-nc" class="language-toggle language-link">ESPAÑOL</a></div></header><section class="problem-hero"><div class="site-shell problem-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Open roof hole and decking repair · Charlotte, NC</p><h1>An open roof needs a safe temporary plan and a layered rebuild.</h1><p>An exposed opening may involve shingles, underlayment, plywood or OSB decking, framing and interior moisture. Majestic first controls access and water, then opens only what is needed to verify the permanent scope.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-gold" href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc#claim-form">Request free inspection →</a><a class="button button-ghost" href="tel:+19808005991">Call Majestic</a></div></div><figure class="problem-hero-visual"><img src="/damage-guides/decking-damage-example.webp" alt="Educational example of an open roof area with deteriorated decking"/><div class="problem-icon problem-icon-decking" aria-label="DECK"><span></span><i></i><b></b></div><figcaption>Educational damage example · inspection determines the actual condition</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="problem-urgent"><div class="site-shell"><strong>SAFETY FIRST</strong><p>Keep everyone out from below an open or sagging area. Do not place weight on exposed decking. Electrical, structural, fire or collapse concerns require the appropriate emergency or licensed specialist first.</p></div></section><section class="problem-signs section"><div class="site-shell problem-clues-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">What you may notice</p><h2>Visible clues help define the inspection—not the final diagnosis.</h2><p>Use these examples to describe what you see from a safe location. A photo cannot confirm every roof layer, hidden moisture, cause or repairability.</p></div><figure class="problem-clue-photo"><img src="/damage-guides/decking-damage-example.webp" alt="Educational example of an open roof area with deteriorated decking"/><figcaption>Educational reference—not a Majestic customer case.</figcaption></figure><ul><li>Visible daylight or open roof covering</li><li>Exposed, split or soft decking</li><li>Sagging between rafters or trusses</li><li>Water entering around a puncture</li><li>Debris, animal or branch penetration</li></ul></div></section><section class="problem-first section" id="first-steps"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Before the crew arrives</p><h2>Five first steps for the homeowner.</h2></div><p>Do only what can be completed safely from the ground or a stable interior area.</p></div><ol><li><span>01</span><p>Restrict access below the opening.</p></li><li><span>02</span><p>Protect belongings only from a safe location.</p></li><li><span>03</span><p>Photograph the opening from the ground or interior without touching it.</p></li><li><span>04</span><p>Call for emergency assessment before more rain.</p></li><li><span>05</span><p>Do not authorize a surface patch without understanding the substrate.</p></li></ol></div></section><section class="problem-process section"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading centered-heading"><p class="eyebrow">How Majestic handles this specific problem</p><h2>A documented path from concern to completed roof.</h2><p>The exact scope depends on safe access and what the inspection confirms. These five stages show how this particular roof condition is evaluated and repaired.</p></div><div class="problem-process-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Safe stabilization</h3><p>We determine whether temporary coverage can be installed safely or whether another trade must stabilize the area.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Controlled opening</h3><p>Loose roofing is removed only as authorized to expose the full boundary of damaged material.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Deck and framing review</h3><p>Affected plywood/OSB and visible framing are documented before replacement.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Layered rebuild</h3><p>Approved decking, underlayment, flashing and roof covering are installed in the correct sequence.</p></article><article><span>05</span><h3>Closeout</h3><p>Final photos identify the repaired area and the customer receives applicable project documents.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="arrival-section section" id="arrival"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">What happens when we arrive</p><h2>Six checkpoints from arrival through closeout.</h2></div><p>Majestic documents the roof as a construction system, explains choices before work begins and keeps insurance coverage decisions separate from contractor work.</p></div><div class="arrival-grid"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Arrival, interview and safety check</h3><p>The technician confirms what happened, when the condition was first noticed, whether water is entering now and which interior rooms are affected. Before using a ladder, Majestic checks weather, electrical, tree, structural and fall hazards and explains any access limitation.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Interior and ground-level reference</h3><p>When relevant and accessible, the team starts at the stain, drip or impacted room, reviews the attic from a safe access point and then walks the exterior perimeter. This creates a reference line between the interior evidence and the roof area above it.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Roof-system inspection</h3><p>When safe access is available, Majestic reviews affected slopes plus shingles, ridge and hip caps, valleys, flashing, pipe boots, vents, skylights, roof edges, gutters, fascia and soffit. Wide photographs show location; detail photographs show the condition.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Measurements and factual documentation</h3><p>The record identifies visible conditions, roof geometry, affected components and estimated quantities. Storm-related observations are separated from age, maintenance, installation details and hidden conditions that cannot be confirmed without authorized removal.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h3>Options explained before authorization</h3><p>Majestic explains immediate protection, localized repair, section rebuild and replacement paths when applicable. The homeowner receives a written roofing path and can choose an out-of-pocket project or use the factual documents in a claim they manage with their carrier.</p></div></article><article><span>06</span><div><h3>Construction, verification and closeout</h3><p>After a written scope is approved, materials and schedule are confirmed. Majestic performs the authorized roofing work, controls debris and cleanup, photographs completion and provides the applicable invoice, warranty and project-closeout documents.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="problem-repairs section" id="repairs"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Repair options</p><h2>The inspection determines which option can be built reliably.</h2></div><p>Final materials, quantities, code requirements and hidden conditions are confirmed in the written scope.</p></div><div class="problem-repair-grid"><article><h3>Plywood or OSB replacement</h3><p>Remove unsound panels to verified boundaries and install code- and system-appropriate sheathing with proper support and fastening.</p></article><article><h3>Framing coordination</h3><p>Rafter, truss or structural damage requires an approved structural repair before decking is closed.</p></article><article><h3>Underlayment and flashing restoration</h3><p>Rebuild the secondary water barrier and all transitions affected by the opening.</p></article><article><h3>Shingle or roof-cover restoration</h3><p>Install compatible field, starter, ridge or metal components; larger replacement is considered when integration is not reliable.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="problem-source"><div class="site-shell"><span>i</span><p>Professional roof repair should address the complete assembly and safe access, not only the visible surface opening. <a href="https://www.gaf.com/en-us/plan-design/homeowner-education/roof-damage/roof-repair" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the source ↗</a></p></div></section><section class="faq-section section"><div class="site-shell faq-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p><h2>Clear expectations before work begins.</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Is the inspection free?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes. Majestic provides a free roof inspection, photographs, a report, estimated measurements and a written project path, subject to safe access.</p></details><details><summary>Does the inspection guarantee insurance coverage?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. Majestic documents roofing conditions and scope. The carrier independently decides coverage and payment.</p></details><details><summary>Can I pay out of pocket?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes. Majestic can explain an out-of-pocket repair or replacement path as well as the construction documentation used for a claim-related project.</p></details><details><summary>How far do you travel?<span>+</span></summary><p>Roof inspections are available approximately 90 minutes from Charlotte or Rock Hill, subject to address and schedule confirmation. Raleigh is not in the service area.</p></details></div></div></section><section class="resource-cta section"><div class="site-shell"><p class="eyebrow">Free inspection</p><h2>Photos, report, estimated measurements and a written project path.</h2><a class="button button-gold" href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc#claim-form">Start my request →</a></div></section><footer class="claim-footer"><div class="site-shell"><a href="/" class="brand brand-footer"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span><strong>MAJESTIC</strong><small>ROOFING, INC.</small></span></a><p>Fully insured · 25+ years of roofing-industry experience across the technical team · English &amp; Spanish</p><a href="tel:+19808005991">(980) 800-5991</a></div></footer>
